+# SAM-6D SLAM Fusion Shadow Evaluation MVP
+
+This package evaluates whether composing SAM-6D object poses with SLAM localization reduces static-object pose jitter. It does not replace SAM-6D production output.
+
+## Local Topic Discovery Basis
+
+- SAM-6D local node: `src/sam6d_ros/sam6d_ros/sam6d_inference_node.py`
+  - PoseArray: `/sam6d_inference/poses`
+  - Configurable 6DoF TransformStamped: default config uses `/sam6d_milk_verify/pose_6dof`
+  - Raw frame: `camera_color_optical_frame`
+  - Current production topics do not publish object score or object id as a separate field. `TransformStamped.child_frame_id` contains `sam6d_object_<id>_<idx>`.
+- ORB-SLAM3 local wrapper: `/home/etri/CLI_environment/orbslam_ws/src/orbslam3_ros2/src/rgbd_node.cpp`
+  - `/orbslam3/pose`, `/orbslam3/odom`, `/orbslam3/tracking_state`, `/tf`
+  - Publishes world to camera TF and camera pose.
+- hdl_graph_slam local ROS2 code: `/home/etri/CLI_environment/hdlgraphslam_ws/src/hdl_graph_slam/src/hdl_graph_slam_ros2/scan_matching_odometry_node.cpp`
+  - `/odom`, `/scan_matching_odometry/transform`, `/scan_matching_odometry/status`, `/tf`
+  - Base/LiDAR branch requires TF from base frame to SAM camera frame.
+- RTAB-Map:
+  - `/home/etri/rtabmap_ws/src/rtabmap_ros` and `/home/etri/rtabmap_ws/config/tiers_indoor02_sauna_rtabmap.yaml` exist outside `CLI_environment`.
+  - Relevant candidates: `/rtabmap/pose`, `/odom`, `/tf`, `/rtabmap/localization_pose`.
+  - `CoreWrapper.cpp` publishes `localization_pose` as `PoseWithCovarianceStamped`; set `rtabmap.pose_topic` to `/rtabmap/localization_pose` and `rtabmap.pose_msg_type` to `pose_with_covariance_stamped` to evaluate that stream.
+
+The node also writes runtime topic presence to `output/sam6d_slam_fusion_shadow_eval/topic_discovery.json`.
+
+## Transform Chains
+
+RGB-D camera SLAM:
+
+```text
+T_WO = T_WC * T_CO
+```
+
+Base/LiDAR SLAM:
+
+```text
+T_WO = T_WB * T_BC * T_CO
+```
+
+If `T_BC` is missing, that branch is marked `not_evaluable_missing_T_BC` and other branches continue.
+
+## Run
+
+Build only the shadow evaluator package:
+
+```bash
+cd /home/etri/CLI_environment/sam6d_jitter_ws
+colcon build --packages-select sam6d_slam_fusion_eval --symlink-install
+source install/setup.bash
+ros2 run sam6d_slam_fusion_eval sam6d_slam_fusion_shadow_eval \
+  --ros-args --params-file src/sam6d_slam_fusion_eval/config/sam6d_slam_fusion_shadow_eval.yaml
+```
+
+Expected outputs:
+
+- `/sam6d/raw_pose_debug`
+- `/sam6d/slam_fused/orbslam3/object_pose_world`
+- `/sam6d/slam_fused/hdl_graph_slam/object_pose_world`
+- `/sam6d/slam_fused/rtabmap/object_pose_world`
+- `/sam6d/slam_fused/orbslam3/object_pose_world_simple_hold_debug`
+- `/sam6d/slam_fused/hdl_graph_slam/object_pose_world_simple_hold_debug`
+- `/sam6d/slam_fused/rtabmap/object_pose_world_simple_hold_debug`
+- `/sam6d/slam_fused/debug_metrics`
+- `output/sam6d_slam_fusion_shadow_eval/sam6d_slam_fusion_shadow_eval.csv`
+- `output/sam6d_slam_fusion_shadow_eval/sam6d_slam_fusion_shadow_eval_report.md`
+
+The default CSV/report filenames are overwritten on each run. Change `output_dir`, `csv_filename`, or `report_filename` when preserving multiple runs.
+
+## CSV Columns
+
+The CSV includes:
+
+```text
+timestamp, frame_id, sam6d_has_pose, sam6d_score, slam_source, slam_has_pose,
+tf_chain_valid, raw_tx, raw_ty, raw_tz, raw_qx, raw_qy, raw_qz, raw_qw,
+world_tx, world_ty, world_tz, world_qx, world_qy, world_qz, world_qw,
+raw_delta_t_mm, raw_delta_r_deg, world_delta_t_mm, world_delta_r_deg,
+fusion_valid, failure_reason
+```
+
+Rows are written for raw SAM-6D, each fused SLAM source, and each simple-hold shadow condition.
+
+## Verdict Rule
+
+- GO: translation jitter is reduced by at least 30%, valid frames are at least 90%, FPS impact is at most 5%, and TF/time sync is usable.
+- WEAK GO: translation jitter is reduced by 10-30% and valid frames are at least 70%.
+- NO-GO: reduction is below 10%, jitter increases, or TF/extrinsic/time sync makes product use risky.
+- INSUFFICIENT_DATA: fewer than two usable samples or no raw baseline.
+
+## Final Decision Questions
+
+The generated report answers:
+
+- Q1. Did ORB-SLAM3 pose fusion reduce jitter?
+- Q2. Did hdl_graph_slam pose fusion reduce jitter?
+- Q3. Did RTAB-Map pose fusion reduce jitter?
+- Q4. Which source has the highest product applicability?
+- Q5. Is SLAM fusion worth applying before One Euro Filter/EKF?
+- Q6. What is the next development step?
+
+## Notes
+
+- This MVP intentionally does not modify SAM-6D ISM/PEM, recall/FP logic, ORB-SLAM3, hdl_graph_slam, or RTAB-Map.
+- `simple_hold` is evaluated only in shadow CSV/report rows. It does not replace SAM-6D output.
+- Set `target_fps_baseline` to estimate FPS impact. If it remains `0.0`, FPS impact is reported as `unknown`.
